---
import { asset, author, repoUrl, treeUrl } from "../data/site";

const links = [
  ["Report", asset("media/vibe_cading_report.pdf"), "M4 2h6l4 4v10H4z M10 2v4h4"],
  ["Code", repoUrl, "M6 5 2 10l4 5 M14 5l4 5-4 5"],
  ["3D models", treeUrl("src/CAD_Harness/sdf/assets/gallery_3d"), "M10 2 3 6v8l7 4 7-4V6z M3 6l7 4 7-4 M10 10v8"],
];
---

<section id="top" class="grid-paper border-b border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 pt-14 pb-12 text-center sm:px-6 sm:pt-20">
    <p class="fig mb-5">TEXT → CAD · OPEN-SOURCE RESEARCH PROJECT</p>
    <h1 class="display text-5xl leading-none font-semibold sm:text-7xl">Vibe-CADing</h1>
    <p class="display mx-auto mt-4 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-snug text-muted sm:text-2xl">
      Conditional CAD Generation and Retrieval for a Text-to-CAD Design Pipeline
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[15px]">
      <a href={author.url} class="font-medium underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-ink">{author.name}</a>
    </p>
    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
      <a href="#try" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-signal bg-signal px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.08em] text-white uppercase transition-opacity hover:opacity-90">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 4l10 6-10 6z" /></svg>
        Try it live
      </a>
      {links.map(([label, href, icon]) => (
        <a href={href} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-line-strong bg-panel/70 px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase transition-colors hover:border-ink">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d={icon} /></svg>
          {label}
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Teaser -->
  <figure class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-14 sm:px-6">
    <div class="frame bg-panel p-2 sm:p-3">
      <span class="corners"></span>
      <img src={asset("media/gallery.gif")} width="880" height="440" class="block w-full"
        alt="Turntables of eight LLM-generated shapes: gear, chess rook, mug, spring, gyroid lattice, rocket, twisted vase and interlocked chain" />
    </div>
    <figcaption class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-3xl text-center text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <span class="font-medium text-ink">Text-to-CAD gallery.</span> Eight prompts (gear, chess rook, mug, spring, gyroid
      lattice, rocket, twisted vase, interlocked chain), each turned into GLSL, validated, rendered and exported as a
      watertight STL.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <!-- Overview -->
  <div class="border-t border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-8 px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[220px_1fr]">
      <div>
        <h2 class="display text-3xl font-semibold">Overview</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          <strong class="font-medium text-ink">Vibe-CADing</strong> is a text-to-CAD pipeline built on one idea:{" "}
          <em class="text-ink">geometry as code</em>. Instead of generating meshes or voxels directly, a language model
          writes a program for the shape: <em class="text-ink">CadQuery</em> or <em class="text-ink">build123d</em> code for
          exact B-rep solids, or a GLSL <em class="text-ink">signed distance function</em> for organic forms. The program
          runs in a sandbox, and every error goes back to the model until the result is valid.
        </p>
        <p>
          A C++ engine turns the code into real parts. It meshes the shape, checks that it can be 3D-printed (wall
          thickness, floating parts, overhangs) and exports STL and glTF. Those checks found flaws that renders hide: a
          chain link printing in mid-air, a lattice falling into 19 loose pieces. The same engine powers a text-to-motion
          demo exported as BVH. Everything below is a file in the repository, failures included.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
